                "text": "While in Starr County this afternoon, I also announced $28,945,000 in federal funding for Union Water Supply Corporation.\n \nThese dollars will go towards expanding and rehabilitating a water treatment plant, ensuring South Texans have clean drinking water.\n \nThank you to Lillian Salerno, USDA Rural Development State Director, Marlene Mendoza, President of the Union Water Supply Board of Directors, and County Commissioner Eloy Garza for working with me to deliver for Starr County!",
