                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Through my work on the Appropriations Committee, I fought to ensure key language was included to strengthen care for veterans facing substance use challenges.\n\u00a0\nThis week, I helped secure $232.9 million to expand Substance Use Disorder treatment at the VA. This funding will enhance provider training and introduce new online tools to better support veterans in recovery.\n\u00a0\nI also helped secure funding for the creation of a new pilot program that applies advanced medical technology to reduce diabetic amputations and prevent insulin-related emergencies. These are life-saving investments for our veteran community.\n\u00a0\nWe owe it to every veteran to deliver the best possible care, and this bill moves us closer to that promise. Proud to work alongside @DeptVetAffairs to support those who\u2019ve served.",
